index 000000000..c8da990da
--- /dev/null
+++ b/support/sqlite-startup-prototype.md
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# Read-only SQLite startup experiment
+
+This branch is an isolated benchmark, not a production storage backend. It is
+based on the descriptor-relative file loader at `47207c800`. No application or
+release packaging enables it.
+
+`sqlite-startup-import.py` imports a disposable configuration tree into SQLite.
+Rows retain relative paths, directory membership/enumeration order, and the exact
+file bytes. The default schema uses a rowid table with indexes on path and on
+parent/order. A WITHOUT ROWID version was also measured: it was substantially
+larger, and its single full-startup observation was slower. Timing variability
+prevents attributing that entire difference to the schema alone.
+
+`src/settings.c` shares its existing JSON/gzip/binary decoding between both read
+paths. The included `sqlite-startup-prototype.c` selects SQLite only when
+`TVH_STARTUP_SQLITE` names a database, and only for paths inside the configured
+settings root. Packaged fallback still uses filebundle. EPG file loading and all
+object creation, scan preparation, linkage and registration are unchanged.
+
+Build with the normal native flags plus SQLite development headers/library:
+
+```sh
+CFLAGS="$(pkg-config --cflags sqlite3)" \
+LDFLAGS="$(pkg-config --libs sqlite3)" ./configure <normal-configure-options>
+make -j4 CFLAGS_NO_WERROR=yes
+python3 support/test-settings-load.py build.linux/tvheadend
+TVH_STARTUP_SQLITE=1 python3 support/test-settings-load.py build.linux/tvheadend
+python3 support/sqlite-startup-import.py /disposable/fixture /disposable/settings.sqlite
+TVH_STARTUP_SQLITE=/disposable/settings.sqlite \
+  ./build.linux/tvheadend -c /disposable/run-copy <normal-test-options>
+```
+
+Keep the imported fixture immutable. Create a fresh run copy for every process.
+Unset the environment variable to exercise the file backend in the same binary.
+Import time and database creation must be measured separately from startup.
+Cold-file-data trials must flush/evict both the run-copy files and the SQLite file;
+this does not drop inode/directory caches or simulate a cold OS boot.
+
+Writes still go to the disposable **file tree**. SQLite is read-only and is not
+updated after edits, rescans or shutdown. Re-import before testing any changed
+configuration. This limitation deliberately excludes normal-operation write
+correctness, migration, crash recovery and durable restart from the experiment.
+Do not enable this prototype for a live configuration. Production adoption needs
+a transactional write path, migration/recovery design and those regression tests.
